<title>USA: Money Store Q1 shr $0.41 vs $0.27.</title>
<headline>Money Store Q1 shr $0.41 vs $0.27.</headline>
<dateline>UNION, N.J. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>THE MONEY STORE INC AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			    Selected Financial Data</p>
<p>		(Dollars in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>Consolidated Statements of Income Data:</p>
<p>							   Three months</p>
<p>							   ended March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	 1996(a)</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p>						    190,468	 134,062</p>
<p> Net income					26,699	  14,204</p>
<p> Net income per share			    0.41	    0.27</p>
<p> Preferred dividends paid		     2,242	     $ -</p>
<p> Common dividends paid			  1,736	   1,078</p>
<p>Note: The company said weighted average number of fully diluted shares was $59.3 million, up 12 percent from the same period a year before. The increase was primarily due to the issuance of 5.9 million shares of common stock in March 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York News desk 212 859-1610</p>
